Changelog: 21-11-2026 20:12:04

Fixed. The app's text is rewritten to the writing standard: its wiki chapter, its README and the text in the window
(tooltips, hints, state lines, the update's messages, the spec sheet and the introduction). Sentences are short, hold
one fact each and no longer chain facts with a colon, a semicolon or parentheses. The README now names the wiki, not
the manual. The question before a firmware update now opens with the question, "Update the <controller> to firmware
<version>?", and gives one fact per line. No label was renamed. One fact was corrected: that question said "The app
saves a backup of the profiles first" for every controller, but the app saves one only for a DualSense Edge, so the
line now shows only for the Edge. The service's two journal lines on a game from Steam now read "A game started from
Steam runs. The controllers stay on." and "The game ended. A controller unused from now on is switched off after the
wait." Nothing the app does has changed. Tests changed: test_idle.py asserts the two journal lines, and
test_main_window.py asserts "The update ends the Bluetooth pairing" in the message after an update. The names nchie,
steffalon, dualsense-edge-profile-web-application and uaccess were added to the text check's word list.

